  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "19c06525-1088-4ba0-8693-aab96f4ba7e4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"\n",
    "    background: linear-gradient(to right, #607d8b, #00bcd4);\n",
    "    color: white;\n",
    "    padding: 0px 10px 1px 10px;\n",
    "    border-radius: 20px;\n",
    "    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n",
    "    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n",
    "    margin: 0;\n",
    "\">\n",
    "<i style=\"color: black; margin-right: 8px;\"></i>\n",
    "    <p>Expanding the <i class=\"fas fa-database\"></i> icon for <code>Data variables:IVT</code> above reveals a table with important information about the Zarr store and the Dask chunking. This summary table shows that a <strong>~38 GB multidimensional dataset is being represented lazily as 367 independently accessible ~105 MB chunks</strong>. This allows Dask to stream only the needed pieces instead of loading the entire dataset into memory.</p>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "20800edf-9d96-4ed1-864d-1d441f90dede",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Check the IVT dataset chunk sizes.  \n",
    "&rarr; **This zarr store is partitoned only temporally, not spatially**. This means that each chunk contains 1000 timesteps for the FULL model domain."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "93c395ad-cfcd-41bf-be90-935c7162a15a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# print(ds.IVT.chunks)\n",
    "print(ds.IVT.chunksizes)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "44d9d8b1-133c-4e3f-9286-5290ba62ac03",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Check file size. Zarr chunks are compressed on disk. HydroShare shows the compressed total (e.g., 24 GiB). `ds.nbytes` reports the uncompressed size of all arrays in the dataset, i.e., what it would take in RAM if loaded."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "13b2a8ec-24aa-4b2c-8a36-9b1b1b6e6e9b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f'Variable size: {ds.nbytes/1e9:.1f} GB')\n",
    "print('Number of years in one file:', round(ds.time.shape[0]/4/365)) "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b5514c86-316a-4f0c-8d0f-63c255f83552",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The **time coordinate in this dataset is not strictly monotonic increasing**, which can break label-based slicing, resampling, and merges. First, check it with the custom function `time_order_report()` and then fix the order:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a8d9b369-4946-417f-a3bf-632c9d78832f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def time_order_report(ds: xr.Dataset, dim: str = \"time\"):\n",
    "    idx = ds.indexes.get(dim)\n",
    "    if idx is None:\n",
    "        raise KeyError(f\"No index found for '{dim}'.\")\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        f\"{dim}: monotonic↑={idx.is_monotonic_increasing}, \"\n",
    "        f\"monotonic↓={idx.is_monotonic_decreasing}, \"\n",
    "        f\"unique={idx.is_unique}, \"\n",
    "        f\"length={len(idx)}\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return idx\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example usage\n",
    "idx = time_order_report(ds)\n",
    "idx"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3e20ba48-c431-47b8-934a-b9fc0a321e3a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# If not strictly increasing or not unique, fix it:\n",
    "ds = ds.sortby(\"time\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Re-check\n",
    "_ = time_order_report(ds)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Start: {ds.time.min().values}\")\n",
    "print(f\"End:   {ds.time.max().values}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "81d48ed8-7e4f-4294-be99-67c40d63a0a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Also, the time axis is a CFTimeIndex, i.e., it uses `cftime` date types for non-Gregorian calendars (e.g., noleap, 360_day). Many plotting and pandas/xarray functions work best with standard NumPy `datetimes`, so we convert to proleptic_gregorian (and drop cftime) before plotting:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1085933f-3ba4-4329-9b7c-f8aaf8258c60",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert to proleptic_gregorian and drop cftime (requires modern xarray)\n",
    "ds = ds.convert_calendar(\"proleptic_gregorian\", use_cftime=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# If there are duplicate timestamps, drop them first (optional but helpful)\n",
    "if ds.get_index(\"time\").has_duplicates:\n",
    "    ds = ds.sel(time=~ds.get_index(\"time\").duplicated())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ba7ea184-8954-400c-a60b-d8b3b1671c22",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "*Note*: This conversion will drop timestamps that do not exist in the Gregorian calendar (e.g., Feb 29 in noleap)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c2debae5-ef22-4edb-90ba-761778cd91b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Subset to a Location and Period of Interest"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ee5822d2-c3c7-4f16-8ce4-6830adc0a519",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Display the full model domain\n",
    "Before we subset the IVT data for a location, let's take a look at the spatial area contained in the Zarr store (_hint: it's very large!_)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "475e1ec3-c5f1-4345-83c1-64935e5f3cbd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# isolate and load in only one timestep of the Zarr store\n",
    "ivt0 = ds.IVT.isel(time=0).compute()\n",
    "\n",
    "# use xarray to inspect metadata attributes of the loaded data\n",
    "print(ivt0.name)\n",
    "print(ivt0.attrs)\n",
    "\n",
    "# compute the bounds of the full model domain (i.e., the Zarr store dataset)\n",
    "bounds = [\n",
    "    [float(ds.lat.min()), float(ds.lon.min())],\n",
    "    [float(ds.lat.max()), float(ds.lon.max())]\n",
    "]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "588027d6-0fc9-4023-ab6a-90706b7130c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Plot the full domain extent of the IVT data for a single timestep. Here, we are using the Python package `cartopy` and accessing a coastline shapefile (`ax.coastlines()`) from the <a href=\"https://www.naturalearthdata.com/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: #1a73e8; text-decoration: underline;\">Natural Earth</a> public domain dataset repository. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "75ac9b37-ed56-4ca9-ac42-d9dabcc97090",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# plot the full extent of the IVT data for one timestep\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(12,8))\n",
    "ax = plt.axes(projection=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n",
    "\n",
    "ivt0.plot(\n",
    "    ax=ax,\n",
    "    transform=ccrs.PlateCarree(),\n",
    "    cmap='viridis',\n",
    "    cbar_kwargs={\"shrink\": 0.6}\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.coastlines()\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"IVT at timestep {ds.time.isel(time=0).values}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a593ff1b-57aa-40dc-a889-d31a09cdabbc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"\n",
    "    background: linear-gradient(to right, #607d8b, #00bcd4);\n",
    "    color: white;\n",
    "    padding: 0px 10px 1px 10px;\n",
    "    border-radius: 20px;\n",
    "    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n",
    "    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n",
    "    margin: 0;\n",
    "\">\n",
    "<i style=\"color: black; margin-right: 8px;\"></i>\n",
    "    <p><i class=\"fas fa-comment\"></i> The <code>cartopy</code> download warning appears the first time you download the coastline shapefiles from Natural Earth because these files are retrieved on demand rather than bundled locally with the Python package.</p>\n",
    "<p>This is conceptually similar to the cloud-native Zarr workflow in this notebook: xarray + Dask access only the specific IVT Zarr metadata and data chunks needed for the current computation or visualization, rather than downloading the full dataset upfront.</p>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4af65c76-e2ba-424a-9db7-479f8cadd87c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Subset IVT for location and time of interest\n",
    "Next, we can subset the IVT for a given location and time period. By default we have selected Bodega Bay (38.3332° N, 123.0481° W), a region frequently impacted by wintertime atmospheric rivers—major drivers of seasonal precipitation and flooding across the Pacific Northwest and Northern California (see https://cw3e.ucsd.edu/heavy-rain-in-the-pacific-northwest/ for more info). In this notebook, we focus on 1970–2009, a late-20th-century subset of the CESM2 LENS historical simulations (1850–2014)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bdfa3671-fcd1-440e-b084-ea60718b012a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "point_name = \"Bodega Bay\"\n",
    "start_date=\"1970-01-01\"\n",
    "end_date=\"2009-12-31\"\n",
    "lat = 38.\n",
    "lon = -123.125 "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fefd3356-0e57-4cca-83c5-41b7539d556a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "m = folium.Map(location=[lat, lon], zoom_start=10)\n",
    "folium.CircleMarker([lat, lon], radius=6, color=\"red\", fill=True, fill_opacity=0.8,\n",
    "                    popup=f\"Lat {lat:.4f}, Lon {lon:.4f}\").add_to(m)\n",
    "m"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "546e64b4-6c14-4b86-ab9e-ed6ff9bf9ac2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"\n",
    "    background: linear-gradient(to right, #607d8b, #00bcd4);\n",
    "    color: white;\n",
    "    padding: 0px 10px 1px 10px;\n",
    "    border-radius: 20px;\n",
    "    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n",
    "    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n",
    "    margin: 0;\n",
    "\">\n",
    "<i style=\"color: black; margin-right: 8px;\"></i>\n",
    "    <p><i class=\"fas fa-comment\"></i> Similar to the on-demand access of the <code>cartopy</code> visualization above, the <code>folium</code> package used here is generating an interactive Leaflet web map and instructs the browser to request only the needed map tiles without downloading the entire map file locally.</p>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "86244344-92f6-4745-80eb-02cb20160e0a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Lazily subset the IVT Zarr store for the time period and point location defined above:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1a2f2d27-afd9-42bb-a04f-a0f6721fb492",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_point = ds.sel(time=slice(start_date, end_date)).sel(lat=lat, lon=lon+360., method='nearest').IVT\n",
    "ds_point"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cdc641fc-a0d0-44be-9b26-cbb5d60e2876",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Load the subsetted data.  \n",
    "&rarr; This step is where we are actually triggering the **retrieval of the selected data chunk into memory**!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "eec65141-490b-4ef0-8c58-53440342da4e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "ds_point = ds_point.load() \n",
    "ds_point.shape\n",
    "\n",
    "# save the dataframe to CSV \n",
    "ds_point.to_dataframe().to_csv(\"ivt_timeseries.csv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "daf659ed-67cf-4812-b102-1a057c6e8781",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Create a timeseries of IVT at the selected lat/lon point:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6bb9d7fb-737b-451a-aaa6-5b0fcf0f88dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "p = (ds_point.hvplot(label='IVT', color='black', line_dash='dashed', line_width=1)\n",
    ").opts(\n",
    "    width=900, height=400, show_grid=True, tools=['hover']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "p  "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7178d3be-223c-40d8-9cc6-b1c6e7dbb598",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Select a set of grid cells around the lat/lon point that cover Bodega Bay, CA (38.3332° N, 123.0481° W)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "64aa84f3-8bdf-495d-bc77-0d82d15f0792",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# the nearest index for the lat/lon provided above\n",
    "ilon = list(ds.lon.values).index(ds.sel(lon=lon+360., method='nearest').lon)\n",
    "ilat = list(ds.lat.values).index(ds.sel(lat=lat, method='nearest').lat)\n",
    "\n",
    "cell_buffer = 10\n",
    "# subset these data to include cells above and below this lat/lon\n",
    "ds_box = ds.sel(time=slice(start_date, end_date)).isel(lat=range(ilat-cell_buffer, ilat+cell_buffer),\n",
    "                  lon=range(ilon-cell_buffer, ilon+cell_buffer)).IVT\n",
    "\n",
    "ds_box = ds_box.to_dataset()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0d3d8d31-972f-4d37-ae10-e1d2cee40022",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Load the subsetted grid cells (and selected data chunks) into memory:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "76262a5f-6dbb-45f8-ae6b-c747b4847cb8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "ds_box = ds_box.load()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "21565aef-3153-435e-b499-859458c0b0e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Plot the IVT data for these cells at time=0 to visualize our domain:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1f7f2728-e063-420b-ab15-693956984f5d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "ax.set_xticks([])\n",
    "ax.set_yticks([])\n",
    "ax = plt.axes(projection=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n",
    "\n",
    "#add coastlines\n",
    "ax.coastlines()\n",
    "\n",
    "#add lat lon grids\n",
    "gl = ax.gridlines(draw_labels=True, color='lightgrey', alpha=0.5, linestyle='--')\n",
    "gl.xlabels_bottom = False\n",
    "gl.ylabels_right = False\n",
    "\n",
    "plot = ds_box.isel(time=0).IVT.plot(label='',\n",
    "                         add_labels=False,\n",
    "                         add_colorbar=False,    \n",
    "                         xticks=None,\n",
    "                         yticks=None)\n",
    "\n",
    "# add custom colorbar inside the figure\n",
    "cbar_ax = fig.add_axes([0.99, 0.25, 0.02, 0.5])  # [left, bottom, width, height] in figure coords\n",
    "cbar = plt.colorbar(plot, cax=cbar_ax)\n",
    "cbar.set_label('IVT (kg m⁻¹ s⁻¹)')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.plot(lon+360., lat,\n",
    "        marker='o', color='red', markersize=8,\n",
    "        transform=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0b360086-08f9-4fb3-ac2e-da35a08e111a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_box"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "093690d6-4ccd-4773-ad05-de7c87490e52",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_box.chunks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "397294da-bff1-4699-9102-e2b9507f29aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Identify Atmospheric River Events"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8516aa57-0965-4bee-8283-93714cdcf9f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To identify atmospheric rivers, we first flag periods where IVT ≥ 250 kg/m/s, a common screening threshold for AR conditions (Ralph et al., 2019). We then classify AR strength into Categories 1–5 using the Ralph et al. (2019) scale, which combines peak IVT and event duration. Lower categories indicate weaker ARs, while higher categories indicate extreme/exceptional events. This workflow is implemented in our Python utility module `ARUtils.py`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b91c0055-f3e9-41f7-abbe-76c60846fcb2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# # Ensure time is a single chunk (so events aren’t broken across chunks)\n",
    "# ds_box = ds_box.chunk({\"time\": -1})\n",
    "# ds_box.chunks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "965f113f-84bd-48b0-970c-3da82a99f8c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Assign an index to each group of timesteps that meet AR conditions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "521e5e34-da09-4465-b946-d971c06a51b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_box['AR_INDEX'] = xr.apply_ufunc(\n",
    "    ARUtils.identify_ar_events,  \n",
    "    ds_box.IVT,  \n",
    "    input_core_dims=[[\"time\"]],\n",
    "    output_core_dims=[[\"time\"]],\n",
    "    vectorize=True,\n",
    "    dask='parallelized',\n",
    "    dask_gufunc_kwargs={'allow_rechunk': True},\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3cfb40c2-b966-4ee3-9881-9454e6ad7b92",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Compute the duration for each AR event"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "91e47765-ecc7-43da-864a-0e6a4c19b133",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_box['AR_DURATION'] = xr.apply_ufunc(\n",
    "    ARUtils.compute_ar_durations,  \n",
    "    ds_box.AR_INDEX,  \n",
    "    input_core_dims=[[\"time\"]],\n",
    "    output_core_dims=[[\"time\"]],\n",
    "    vectorize=True,\n",
    "    dask='parallelized',\n",
    "    dask_gufunc_kwargs={'allow_rechunk': True},\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aff75289-e738-4cd0-abc3-6ef0b77928ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Compute the category (1-5) for each AR event"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "66106031-7875-4bc8-8347-b6a1fd1ed6b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_box['AR_CATEGORY'] = xr.apply_ufunc(\n",
    "    ARUtils.compute_ar_category,  \n",
    "    ds_box.AR_INDEX,\n",
    "    ds_box.AR_DURATION,\n",
    "    ds_box.IVT,\n",
    "    input_core_dims=[[\"time\"],[\"time\"],[\"time\"]],\n",
    "    output_core_dims=[[\"time\"]],\n",
    "    vectorize=True,\n",
    "    dask='parallelized',\n",
    "    dask_gufunc_kwargs={'allow_rechunk': True},\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9dabec07-139f-41b3-8ec0-c78bf4929d81",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Compute the probability of each AR event occurring"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e826ec5f-fe4e-4ecf-a11f-94c1920c8d64",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "res = xr.apply_ufunc(\n",
    "    ARUtils.compute_ar_probability,\n",
    "    ds_box.AR_INDEX,\n",
    "    ds_box.AR_CATEGORY,\n",
    "    input_core_dims=[[\"time\"],[\"time\"]],\n",
    "    output_core_dims=[['category']],\n",
    "    # output_sizes={'category': 5},\n",
    "    output_dtypes=[float],\n",
    "    vectorize=True,\n",
    "    dask='parallelized',\n",
    "    dask_gufunc_kwargs={'allow_rechunk': True,\n",
    "                        'output_sizes': {'category': 5}},\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add the category dimension (from 1 to 5)\n",
    "res = res.assign_coords(category=np.arange(1, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# add the newly computed probabilty back to the original dataset\n",
    "ds = ds.assign(AR_PROBABILITY=res)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d65bb0ac-9226-4b0f-89e8-dc15af1ad5ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Compute the magnitude of each AR event."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0ab419e4-0ca2-4cbf-8bf9-d314bdfbe8a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_box['AR_DEGREE'] = xr.apply_ufunc(\n",
    "    ARUtils.compute_ar_degree,\n",
    "    ds_box.IVT,\n",
    "    ds_box.AR_DURATION,\n",
    "    ds_box.AR_INDEX,\n",
    "    input_core_dims=[[\"time\"],[\"time\"],[\"time\"]],\n",
    "    output_core_dims=[['time']],\n",
    "    output_dtypes=[float],\n",
    "    vectorize=True,\n",
    "    dask='parallelized',\n",
    "    dask_gufunc_kwargs={'allow_rechunk': True},\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "77c142c4-cf39-4d67-9ffe-0d0fe151bb7d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Plot Computed AR Category"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a07b1c84-574d-4dae-81b5-7a00bc3f4f09",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Mean Atmospheric Rivers category through the record of data. Let's first build contour plots of mean AR_CATEGORY for each decade in our dataset using `cartopy`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9e522c3d-ea83-4d14-8af7-b4bde7e37735",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "year = ds_box[\"time\"].dt.year\n",
    "decade = np.floor(year / 10) * 10\n",
    "ds_box = ds_box.assign_coords({'decade':decade})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4283c14a-9ba0-48ee-92e4-eda2c156712d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_decade = ds_box.where(ds_box.AR_CATEGORY > 0) \\\n",
    "            .AR_CATEGORY \\\n",
    "            .groupby('decade') \\\n",
    "            .mean(dim='time').compute()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c29bdb9f-40bb-4298-b986-8593099e68c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(nrows=2, ncols=2,\n",
    "                       subplot_kw={'projection': ccrs.PlateCarree()},\n",
    "                       figsize=(10,8),\n",
    "                       layout='constrained')\n",
    "\n",
    "axes = ax.flatten()\n",
    "for i in range(0, len(ds_decade.decade)):\n",
    "    axes[i].coastlines();\n",
    "    axes[i].gridlines(draw_labels=True, color='lightgrey', alpha=0.5, linestyle='--');\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # created grid and contour plots.\n",
    "    d_plot = ds_decade.isel(decade=i).plot(label='',\n",
    "                   add_labels=False,\n",
    "                   add_colorbar=False,                   \n",
    "                   ax=axes[i])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    c_plot = ds_decade.isel(decade=i).plot.contour(add_labels=True,\n",
    "                                                   add_colorbar=False,\n",
    "                                                   colors='white',\n",
    "                                                   ax=axes[i])\n",
    "    axes[i].clabel(c_plot)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "    st = int(ds_decade.decade[i].item())\n",
    "    et = st + 9\n",
    "    axes[i].set_title(f'{st} - {et}')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.colorbar(d_plot, ax=ax[:, 1], shrink=0.8);\n",
    "fig.suptitle('Mean Decadal AR Category');"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "28970279-661f-45b8-b696-de6ade016d22",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Build contour plots of mean AR_DEGREE for each decade in our dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3b2433ba-d240-4ae9-b980-dde039b89296",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ds_decade = ds_box.where(ds_box.AR_CATEGORY > 0) \\\n",
    "            .AR_DEGREE \\\n",
    "            .groupby('decade') \\\n",
    "            .mean(dim='time').compute()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2989c64d-ffe7-4088-84d7-be123d1b7102",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.ticker as ticker\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(nrows=2, ncols=2,\n",
    "                       subplot_kw={'projection': ccrs.PlateCarree()},\n",
    "                       figsize=(10,8),\n",
    "                       layout='constrained')\n",
    "\n",
    "axes = ax.flatten()\n",
    "for i in range(0, len(ds_decade.decade)):\n",
    "    axes[i].coastlines();\n",
    "    axes[i].gridlines(draw_labels=True, color='lightgrey', alpha=0.5, linestyle='--');\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # created grid and contour plots.\n",
    "    d_plot = ds_decade.isel(decade=i).plot(label='',\n",
    "                   add_labels=False,\n",
    "                   add_colorbar=False,                   \n",
    "                   ax=axes[i])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    c_plot = ds_decade.isel(decade=i).plot.contour(add_labels=True,\n",
    "                                                   add_colorbar=False,\n",
    "                                                   colors='white',\n",
    "                                                   ax=axes[i])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # custom formatting function for contour labels on the maps\n",
    "    def fmt_func(value):\n",
    "        return f'{value:.0e}'\n",
    "        \n",
    "        \n",
    "    axes[i].clabel(c_plot, inline=True, fontsize=10, fmt=fmt_func)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "    st = int(ds_decade.decade[i].item())\n",
    "    et = st + 9\n",
    "    axes[i].set_title(f'{st} - {et}')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.colorbar(d_plot, ax=ax[:, 1], shrink=0.8);\n",
    "fig.suptitle('Mean Decadal AR Degree');"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8412ea80-cf9a-4dab-89ed-16d27da435f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### 🎉 Save the Mean Decadal AR Degree Figure for our HydroShare Resource!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d698aa1d-784a-4a6e-aa28-45bd9514c6f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig.savefig(\n",
    "    \"mean_decadal_ar_degree.png\",\n",
    "    dpi=150,\n",
    "    bbox_inches=\"tight\"\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5dcac133-d881-4314-bbf6-2cb46cce3a49",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Push data back into HydroShare"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7e7ab13b-ca1d-448b-80e8-55facfebddcd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now that we have extracted, analyzed and visualized our data of interest, we can push the data back to HydroShare in a new resource through the Python client for the HydroShare API called `hsclient`. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8b0df623-6a6c-4838-b723-1d937c694e0d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Create a New Empty Resource\n",
    "\n",
    "The following code can be used to create a new, empty resource within which you can create content and metadata.It also creates an in-memory object representation of that resource in your local environmment that you can then manipulate with further code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cfa5b699-7706-433e-acc6-e4efd08d0144",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create the new, empty resource\n",
    "new_resource = hs.create()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get the HydroShare identifier for the new resource\n",
    "res_identifier = new_resource.resource_id\n",
    "print(f'The HydroShare Identifier for your new resources is: {res_identifier}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Construct a hyperlink to access the HydroShare landing page for the new resource\n",
    "print(f'Your new resource is available at: {new_resource.metadata.url}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5b720a0b-71e2-479c-8024-83b5a2a10322",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Creating and Editing Resource Metadata Elements\n",
    "\n",
    "We can first add metadata to our resource. Editing metadata elements for a resource can be done in an object oriented way. You can specify all of the metadata elements in code, which will set their values in memory in your local environment. Values of metadata elements can be edited, removed, or replaced by setting them to a new value, appending new values (in the case where the metadata element accepts a list), or by removing the value entirely. \n",
    "\n",
    "When you are ready to save edits to metadata elements from your local environment to the resource in HydroShare, you can call the `save()` function on your resource and all of the new metadata values you created/edited will be saved to the resource in HydroShare. Note that by default you are listed as the author and owner of a newly created resource. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0eae1da3-1efb-4727-9fae-b696e28f9ce5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Print the Creator names\n",
    "print('The list of Authors includes: ')\n",
    "for creator in new_resource.metadata.creators:\n",
    "    if creator.name is None:\n",
    "        print(creator.organization)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(creator.name)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "47efaedd-3f7a-4b89-b9fd-53da765634f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Resource Title and Abstract\n",
    "\n",
    "The Title and Abstract metadata elements can be specified as text strings. To modify the Title or Abstract after it has been set, just set them to a different value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "58a301ce-a85e-4437-be6d-fa8191874dcd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Set the Title for the resource\n",
    "new_resource.metadata.title = f'Integrated Vapor Transport - {point_name}'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set the Abstract text for the resource\n",
    "new_resource.metadata.abstract = (\n",
    "    'This resource contains integrated vapor transport (IVT) data'\n",
    "    'for a selected location and time period. The outputs were generated from a '\n",
    "    'notebook that subsets cloud-hosted IVT data and summarizes changes in atmospheric '\n",
    "    'moisture transport at the specified point.'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Call the save function to save the metadata edits to HydroShare\n",
    "new_resource.save()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print the title just added to the resource\n",
    "print(f'Title: {new_resource.metadata.title}')\n",
    "print(f'Abstract: {new_resource.metadata.abstract}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "56e5a368-da56-4e59-8547-abadfbd48aa1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Subject Keywords\n",
    "\n",
    "Subject keywords can be specified as a Python list of strings. Keywords can be added by creating a list, appending new keywords to the existing list, or by overriding the existing list with a new one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cb2669b4-b941-42ed-89a0-e9325f2d15dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create subject keywords for the resource using a list of strings\n",
    "new_resource.metadata.subjects = ['Atmospheric Rivers', 'Integrated vapor transport', 'Hydroinformatics']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save the changes to the resource in HydroShare\n",
    "new_resource.save()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print the keywords for the resource\n",
    "print('The list of keywords for the resource includes:')\n",
    "for keyword in new_resource.metadata.subjects:\n",
    "    print(keyword)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "90a07417-68a7-460e-8c03-44fb73ab755e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Spatial and Temporal Coverage\n",
    "\n",
    "Initially the spatial and temporal coverage for a resource are empty. To set them, you have to create a coverage object of the right type and set the spatial or temporal coverage to that object."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7e5e40c2-5308-4bbd-bfcc-fb8ae16dfe8d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import the required metadata classes for coverage objects\n",
    "from hsmodels.schemas.fields import BoxCoverage, PointCoverage, PeriodCoverage\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "\n",
    "# If you want to set the spatial coverage to a PointCoverage instead\n",
    "new_resource.metadata.spatial_coverage = PointCoverage(name=point_name,\n",
    "                                                       north=lat,\n",
    "                                                       east=lon,\n",
    "                                                       projection='WGS 84 EPSG:4326',\n",
    "                                                       type='point',\n",
    "                                                       units='Decimal degrees')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a beginning and ending date for a time period\n",
    "beginDate = datetime.strptime(start_date,'%Y-%m-%d')\n",
    "endDate = datetime.strptime(end_date,'%Y-%m-%d')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set the temporal coverage of the resource to a PeriodCoverage object\n",
    "new_resource.metadata.period_coverage = PeriodCoverage(start=beginDate,\n",
    "                                                       end=endDate)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save the changes to the resource in HydroShare\n",
    "new_resource.save()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print the temporal coverage information\n",
    "print('Temporal Coverage:')\n",
    "print(new_resource.metadata.period_coverage)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print the spatial coverage information\n",
    "print('\\nSpatial Coverage:')\n",
    "print(new_resource.metadata.spatial_coverage)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4c112c2c-ab89-4bbd-bc24-6d89cf829c33",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Funding Agency Credits\n",
    "\n",
    "Funding agency information contains multiple attributes when you add a funding agency to a HydroShare resource. You can create multiple funding agency entries for a resource, which get stored as a Python list. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a2fe3bb7-c3eb-4227-86c2-9048f0e78455",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a new AwardInfo object\n",
    "newAwardInfo = AwardInfo(funding_agency_name='National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA)',\n",
    "                         title=('Cooperative Institute for Research to Operations in HydrologyCooperative Institute for Research to Operations in Hydrology'),\n",
    "                         number='NA22NWS4320003')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Append the new AwardInfo object to the list of funding agencies\n",
    "new_resource.metadata.awards.append(newAwardInfo)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save the changes to the resource in HydroShare\n",
    "new_resource.save()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print the AwardInfo\n",
    "print('Funding sources added: ')\n",
    "for award in new_resource.metadata.awards:\n",
    "    print(f'Award Title: {award.title}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "69cb0ae2-27b2-478e-9426-1643c1c95a0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Adding Files to a Resource\n",
    "\n",
    "In this section we will add the content files directly to the resource! Note that if you upload files that already exist, those files will be overwritten."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "72b5e665-7199-4618-b507-c72b62c7ee6f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# We can add both mean decadal AR figure and the point-based IVT \n",
    "# timeseries data to the HydroShare resource\n",
    "new_resource.file_upload('mean_decadal_ar_degree.png')\n",
    "new_resource.file_upload('ivt_timeseries.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print the names of the files in the resource\n",
    "print('Updated file list after adding a file: ')\n",
    "for file in new_resource.files(search_aggregations=True):\n",
    "    print(file.path)"
   ]
  }
